SOAPBOX: This time out it was just me and my ?100 watts and a wire? pea
SOAPBOX: shooter station. Add to that a Murphy running rampant through
SOAPBOX: the clover and you have the makings for a frustrating weekend.
SOAPBOX: This was my first real attempt at SO2R contest operation. FT*
SOAPBOX: is a near-perfect match for this style as it has well defined
SOAPBOX: intervals for TX and RX. My Flex-6600 made it dead easy to setup
SOAPBOX: two slices on two antennas feeding N1MM configured for SO2R. I
SOAPBOX: had tested this setup a few times and found it worked well.
SOAPBOX: Well, that was then.
SOAPBOX: It wasn't long before Murphy arrived. It
SOAPBOX: was subtle things. N1MM would be logging fine, but the clock
SOAPBOX: stopped updating... and the online scoreboard stopped updating...
SOAPBOX: the info window stopped updating... and JTAlert started adding 6
SOAPBOX: character grid IDs. ARGH! Also, the N1MM - WSJT-X connection
SOAPBOX: window turned red as if WSJTX had crashed - it had not. Seeing
SOAPBOX: that the log was being recorded I pressed on. After a time, N1MM
SOAPBOX: become unresponsive and I restarted the PC. It would be fine for
SOAPBOX: a short while but eventually the symptoms would return. UGH!
SOAPBOX: Rinse/Repeat.
SOAPBOX: FT4 was quite active this time out which made for
SOAPBOX: a much more enjoyable rate. However I quickly discovered the
SOAPBOX: shortcomings of my pea shooter station I heard lots of people
SOAPBOX: but many did not hear me. Perhaps I could replace signal
SOAPBOX: strength with BIC time? After a lackluster 13hr shift I opted
SOAPBOX: for some sleep. Back at it at ~10Z for a final push to the end.
SOAPBOX: 40M FT4 was a real surprise - lots of activity and 77 Qs. The
SOAPBOX: other FT4 bands were active but not as productive. 10M was a
SOAPBOX: complete bust as has been the pattern of late. 20 & 15M FT8 were
SOAPBOX: the money spots with ~140 Qs each. A few highlights were VU2DX,
SOAPBOX: ZP4MNB, 2 x ZLs, TI1M (for obvious reasons), DV1K, BI4KYT, and
SOAPBOX: 9J2FI.
SOAPBOX: Clearly I have some troubleshooting to do ? and perhaps
SOAPBOX: some antenna work. Hey, if it were easy everyone could do it!
SOAPBOX: 73 & thanks for the Qs!
